<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Javanese War of Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1719–1723</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Javanese War of Succession (1719–1723) followed the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakubuwana-i">Pakubuwana I</a> of Mataram, when brothers and uncles of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amangkurat-iv">Amangkurat IV</a> rebelled against the new king. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> supported Amangkurat IV, defeated the rebels and exiled several princes. The war confirmed the Company as the arbiter of the Mataram succession.</p></div>
